Third-party components

The directory `challenge-generation/` contains the chgen library, which is
not the work of the author of this dissertation. It originates from the
ctf4ed project (https://github.com/ctf4ed/chgen), authored by
Roberto Metere (Newcastle University, 2019) and Charles Morisset
(2021-2024), and is distributed under the MIT License. The original
LICENSE and README files are retained at `challenge-generation/LICENSE`
and `challenge-generation/README.md` respectively. The file headers on
`challenge-generation/chgen.js` and `challenge-generation/deploy/alpine_deploy.js`
preserve the original authors' copyright notices.

The per-CTF generator scripts under `CTFs/challenge-generation/`
(`chgen_ctf<n>.js`, `generators/<ctf>_generator.js`,
`generate_credentials.js`) are original work by the author of this
dissertation, but they extend and depend on the chgen library above.
They follow the chgen convention of subclassing `ChallengeGenerator`
and overriding `processTemplate` to produce per-player CTF variants.
Without the upstream chgen library, those scripts will not run.

All other directories of this repository (`CTFs/<CTF_dir>/` aside from
the per-CTF `challenge-generation/` scripts, `Evaluation/`, `report/`,
and the root tooling) are the work of the dissertation author and are
released under the MIT License above.
